/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (COVID-19 Accelerated Digital Adoption and Became a Turning Point for Fintech Growth The COVID-19 pandemic accelerated the global fintech industry by boosting demand for digital financial services. Valued at about USD 111 billion in 2019, the sector grew to nearly USD 136 billion by 2021 as lockdowns drove adoption of digital banking, mobile wallets, and contactless payments. This shift made fintech a mainstream alternative to traditional banking and laid the foundation for its current double-digit CAGR.)
/E (COVID-19 Accelerated Digital Adoption and Became a Turning Point for Fintech Growth The COVID-19 pandemic accelerated the global fintech industry by boosting demand for digital financial services. Valued at about USD 111 billion in 2019, the sector grew to nearly USD 136 billion by 2021 as lockdowns drove adoption of digital banking, mobile wallets, and contactless payments. This shift made fintech a mainstream alternative to traditional banking and laid the foundation for its current double-digit CAGR.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
