endobj
462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A strategic sale of Wise to a global payments company such as Visa, Mastercard, PayPal, or a large international bank is feasible, given the strong synergies in regulatory licenses, technology, and customer base. However, such a transaction would face significant hurdles, as approvals across 160+ jurisdictions and potential antitrust scrutiny could delay or even block the deal. Moreover, private equity investors may forgo the valuation upside available in public markets, where fintech companies are typically rewarded with higher growth multiples. A secondary sale to another private equity fund or a sovereign wealth fund represents a reliable fallback option, as it provides liquidity if IPO markets are unfavorable. But this is usually a fallback option, since valuations in secondary sales tend to be lower than those achieved through IPO exits.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
